Answer: Consider:

```java
add(3.1F, 3.2F);
```

The following method executes:

```java
public static float add(float a, float b) {
return a + b;
}
```

The F suffix makes both arguments float.

Answer: Consider:

```java
add(2.111, 3.333);
```

The following method executes:

```java
public static double add(double a, double b) {
return a + b;
}
```

Decimal literals without the F suffix are treated as double.

